 a/Outline.md b/Outline.md\nindex 7288d5c..3c76398 100644\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n # Outline — how many benchmarks must be run, which ones, and when does it hold\n \n-*Rev. 4, by story-repo (see the revision log). Built from the `Brief` (idea-repo, rev. 5) and the objective (`story-repo`#1). It says what to test and which figure carries which claim; it never says what a result must be. Each claim has a branch for the case it fails — a failing claim is reported as a finding, not repaired.*\n+*Rev. 4, by story-repo (see the revision log). Built from the `Brief` (idea-repo, rev. 6) and the pre-registration (`experiment-repo` `prereg/PREREG.md`, commit 7731e49) and the objective (`story-repo`#1). It says what to test and which figure carries which claim; it never says what a result must be. Each claim has a branch for the case it fails — a failing claim is reported as a finding, not repaired.*\n \n ## 0. Working title and scope line\n \"How many benchmarks must you run? Choosing and sizing the run set that predicts a new model's other scores — evidence from embedding-model leaderboards\".\n@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@ Every claim is stated so that it can fail. \"Analysis owns the method and whether\n Evidence: the spectrum of the filtered matrix with the noise reference; r by the three estimators; held-out CV error vs rank.\n If it fails (no clear r, estimators disagree widely): the paper says so and the curve in C2 is described through the spectrum's decay (T2 second regime); no \"rank-r\" language.\n \n-**C2 — The needed k (headline, Q).** On whole held-out groups, standardised and raw-point error of S6+P5 as k grows approaches the floor (all of the model's observed cells in C given, scored on the same T); the smallest k reaching ε (ε = δ and 2δ) is the number the paper reports, with group-bootstrap CI, with k on the axis and k/N alongside; headline k ≤ ⌊|C|/2⌋ on the pool (≈ N/3 once |T| ≈ N/3; k/N on the axis), larger k only as a labelled supplement.\n+**C2 — The needed k (headline, Q).** On whole held-out groups, standardised and raw-point error of S6+P5 as k grows approaches the floor (all of the model's observed cells in C given, scored on the same T); the smallest k whose **excess over the model's own all-others floor** (same target cells) is ≤ ε (ε = δ and 2δ; an absolute error ≤ δ is unreachable because δ ≤ 0.25 × floor — pre-registration §F) is the number the paper reports, with group-bootstrap CI, with k on the axis and k/N alongside; headline k ≤ ⌊|C|/2⌋ on the pool (≈ N/3 once |T| ≈ N/3; k/N on the axis), larger k only as a labelled supplement.\n Evidence: error vs k with CIs on (a) the group-held-out split **scored on the common target set (§2b)**, (b) the fixed subset of models eligible at k_max (≥ k_max observed cells in C and ≥ m_T in T, in the same splits), so the model set does not change along the axis; the all-eligible-per-k curve is a labelled supplement; (c) number of eligible models and (model, split) pairs per k and for the floor (eligibility rule: Brief rev. 5); baselines k=1,2,3 vs the mean-offset (general-factor) baseline stated explicitly.\n If it fails (floor not reached at the largest headline k): the finding is \"the headline k range is not enough in this matrix\", with the misfit decomposition saying why.\n \n@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ Evidence: primary-contrast table; secondary selection rules S1–S5, S7, S8 (and\n Story branches (both are publishable, the abstract is written after the verdict): (A) design helps below ~r and the gap closes after; (B) random-k is equivalent past very small k and the paper's message becomes \"needed k ≈ r+Δ, no selection needed\", with T1/T2 explaining why. If the verdicts are \"undecided\" for mos\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "f00aad4e-f899-5dbe-82a6-514e8cff7f47", "at": 1795730062.6442888, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 17010, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission